          "evidence": "The horizontal axis is labeled 'Advertising Spend ($ thousands)' and the vertical axis is labeled 'Sales ($ thousands)'.",
          "status": "supported"
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "evidence": "The five labeled points (Store 6 through Store 10) show a clear positive correlation, with each successive store positioned further right and higher than the previous.",
          "status": "supported"
        }
      ],
      "B": {
        "reading_checked": "If the horizontal axis encodes advertising spend and the vertical axis encodes sales on the printed comparable scales, then points farther right and higher represent stores with greater plotted spend and greater plotted sales; this is an association only, not proof that spend caused sales or that expansion is profitable.",
        "evidence": "The axis labels and the plotted points' positions directly support the decoding that higher points represent greater spend and sales. The conclusion that this is an association only is a standard statistical interpretation of the visible data.",
